From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:08:54 +0900
Subject: Folio: landscape keeps the grid and the widgets' shape,
 the row/column swap is a setting

In landscape Folio turned the page (RotateCounterClockwise: rows and columns swapped, each
widget's width and height swapped), so a 4x1 bar widget became a 1x4 sliver too narrow for its
text. Launcher3 and One UI keep a phone's grid in landscape with wider, lower cells and hide the
app names; the folio README lists "option to turn off row/column swap" as a wanted feature. Now
the swap is the setting swapRowsColumnsInLandscape (off by default, in the home screen settings
with its Simplified Chinese text): off, landscape keeps the page as it is (RegularPosition) and
the home screen's app names are hidden there, the cells being too low for them. The stored
layout is the same either way.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-01
X-Rungic-Status: Pending
X-Rungic-Tests: none (gap: checked on the phone, docs/50)
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/50
